WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.901
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:06.100
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:08.601
Well, let's get to some news.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.167
Guys, President Biden
is wrapping up

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.834
his first trip to Asia
since taking office

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:16.267
after spending a few days
in South Korea and Japan.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:17.934
So, if you're keeping track,

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:21.133
there's a drought out West,
inflation is still headed north,

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:22.467
Biden's in the Far East,

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.868
and his approval rating
is down south.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:27.634
But Biden's trip is going well.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.701
So far, he's only made one
statement that The White House

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:32.367
had to immediately walk back.

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.367
Biden spent the weekend
in South Korea,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.133
and you could tell he really
started to pick up on

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.167
South Korean culture.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.167
Watch this.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:42.334
♪♪

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.901
-Smooth like butter.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.067
Like a criminal under cover.

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.133
Gonna pop like trouble.

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.868
Breaking into your
heart like that.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:50.968
-Yeah.
[ Cash register dings ]

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.834
Not bad.
He was just getting into it.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.200
-Yeah.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.434
-Of course, a big focus of
Biden's trip

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.434
to Asia is the threat of
North Korea.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.000
And yesterday,
when a reporter asked Biden

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.734
if he had a message for
Kim Jong-un, he said,

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.701
"Hello. Period."

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.934
That sounds like a grandpa
trying to send a voice text.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:17.334
Like, "Hello. Period.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.567
Happy birthday. Stop."

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:23.167
Yep, Biden said he's open to
meeting with Kim Jong-un

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:26.367
if Kim is "sincere and serious."

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:29.167
And Kim was like, "Oh, I think
I gave you the wrong idea.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:32.067
I'm just looking to have
fun hookups this summer."

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.434
Yep, sincere and serious.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.467
That sounds like a
"Fast and the Furious" spin-off

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.367
for your mom.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:41.334
Meanwhile, North Korea could be
resuming nuclear tests

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.334
for the first time
in nearly five years.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.667
But Biden said
he's not concerned.

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.367
Yep. That's how things are
going right now.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.567
North Korea is launching a nuke,

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.634
and it's like eighth on
Biden's to-do list.

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.067
He's like, "Yeah, okay."

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.300
Yep, on his trip to Asia,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.400
Biden has talked about
a wide range of issues.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.634
And I thought he had some pretty
interesting things to say.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:58.667
Here's Biden at a meeting.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.601
Interesting. I just -- I don't
know what he's talk--

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.067
-Wow!
-It's just interesting.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.467
Next, here he is at a dinner.
Listen to this.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:39.367
I just...

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:40.767
It's just interesting,
what he says.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.367
-Licorice soda.
-Wow.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:44.400
-Here he is touring
a Samsung factory.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.434
Listen to this.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.167
It's just interesting.

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:05.133
Well, switching gears,
today, Starbucks

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.801
announced that after 15 years
in business,

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:11.501
they're closing down all 130
of their cafés in Russia

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.067
and leaving permanently.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.400
That's a tough break
for Russians,

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.067
because they were just a month
away from their favorite

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.400
coffee release,
the Putin-spiced latte.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.868
Yeah. Well, some business news.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.067
I read that Applebee's
doesn't want its restaurants

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.634
taking pickup orders
over the phone anymore.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:28.567
So it's setting up call centers
to do it for them.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:29.734
Actually,
there's several restaurants

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:31.300
that use call centers,
and each one

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.467
has a very unique greeting
when you call.

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.133
For example,
here's the Applebee's greeting.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.033
Yeah, pretty standard stuff.

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.567
Then here's Benihana's greeting.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.634
-Wow!

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.801
-Next, here's the greeting from
Tommy Bahama.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.501
-♪ Are you reelin'
in the years ♪

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:09.767
♪ Stowin' away the time ♪

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.300
-Yeah, it's pretty good.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.000
And, finally, here's the
greeting for Chuck E. Cheese.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.033
-Chuck E. Cheese.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.868
Interesting. Wow.

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:23.467
They're all different.

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:26.934
Well, get this.

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:28.567
I saw that Hot Pockets
is coming out with

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:31.701
a new thaw-and-eat sandwich.

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:33.601
So instead of using
the microwave,

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.000
you just take it
out of the freezer

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.467
and let it sit for a few hours.

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.634
Mmm!

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:44.100
Nothing more delicious than
a room-temperature pocket.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.133
You can't win with Hot Pockets.

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:48.133
You either have to wait
three hours for them to cool off

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.400
or three hours
for them to heat up.

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:53.000
Oh, I heard --
Guys, check this out.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.367
I heard that authorities
in the Midwest

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:57.167
are on the lookout for TikTokers
who have damaged property

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.934
while doing something called the
Kool-Aid Man Challenge.

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:01.067
Take a look at this.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.133
-It's called the
Kool-Aid Man Challenge,

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.701
and it's recently gone viral
in Nebraska.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:08.067
Teens are running
into fences, saying,

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.334
"Oh, yeah!"
like the Kool-Aid Man

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:11.801
and knocking the fence down.

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.133
-Yeah.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:15.400
It's pretty serious.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.334
So here now via satellite to
discuss the trend is

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.701
the guy who started it all,
Kool-Aid Man.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:23.133
Kool-Aid Man, are you there?
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:25.467
-Alright.
Thank you for being here.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:26.934
Do you use TikTok?

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:29.167
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.100
-And so you've seen
the Kool-Aid Man challenge.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.934
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.267
-So you agree it's dangerous.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.067
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.634
-Do you think the people
who have knocked down fences

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:38.801
should have to pay for them?

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:41.367
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.868
Is that all you
have to say about it?

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:44.801
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:46.334
-I guess you have
to be careful of what you say,

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:47.801
in case anyone
decides to sue you.

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:49.400
-Oh, yeah!
-Yeah, alright.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.133
Hey, real quick, before you go,
I always wanted to know this.

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:52.968
What kind of Kool-Aid
is in your pitcher?

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:55.133
-It's actually my blood, Jimmy.

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:57.100
I'm just a pitcher of blood.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.968
But when you think about it,
aren't we all?

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:01.434
-Kool-Aid Man, everyone.

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:07.300
Hey, did you guys
hear about this?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.033
Jif peanut butter
is being recalled

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.300
for potential salmonella
contamination.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.901
Yep, they're offering
two options.

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:16.100
You can either have salmonella
or chunky salmonella.

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:18.000
Hey, this is interesting.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.434
I read that the average American

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:23.033
spends $314 every month
on impulse buys.

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:24.234
Yeah. I don't know.

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:26.167
That sounds kind of high,
don't you think, Higgins?

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:29.868
[ Whirring ]
-You know what?

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:32.367
People have got to be better
with the summer money out there.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.834
-Yeah.
-Hold on a second. Wait.

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:36.000
-Yep.
[ Alarm chirps ]

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.267
-Had to unlock my Jet Ski.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:40.367
Appreciate it.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.767
Thank you, Steve.

00:06:43.767 --> 00:06:46.267
Guys, I saw that the producers
of "90 Day Fiancé"

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:48.701
are coming out with a new show
that will follow couples

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.434
who are trying to
run restaurants

00:06:50.434 --> 00:06:51.534
while keeping their
relationships

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:53.167
from falling apart.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.901
Yeah, the show
is going to be called

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:58.334
"Diners, Divorce and Dives."

00:06:58.334 --> 00:06:59.701
Hey, well, get this.

00:06:59.701 --> 00:07:02.601
According to a new survey,
new parents Google more than

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:06.300
2,000 baby questions
in their child's first year.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.667
Yeah, Google
actually released some of

00:07:07.667 --> 00:07:10.133
the most common baby questions
people search for.

00:07:10.133 --> 00:07:11.968
Here are just a few.
First up, there's...

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.000
Next, there's...

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.467
After that, we have...

00:07:22.801 --> 00:07:25.033
Next up is...

00:07:28.133 --> 00:07:29.601
And then there's...

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:33.100
After that, we have...

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:36.834
Followed by...

00:07:39.467 --> 00:07:40.634
After that, we have...

00:07:42.601 --> 00:07:43.667
And finally...

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:46.601
There you go.

00:07:46.601 --> 00:07:50.200
Very...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.067
-Wow!

00:07:53.067 --> 00:07:54.200
-Some local news.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.934
I saw that New York City's
last remaining

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:59.334
public pay-phone booth
was just removed.

00:07:59.334 --> 00:08:00.601
That headline again.

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:03.968
New York City has removed
its last public restroom.

